---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Steps from '../components/Steps.astro';
import Journey from '../components/Journey.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base title="How it works: set up in 3 steps" description="Set up OKtoPress in 3 steps: sign up, set prices from a starter grid, and paste one line of code or install the WordPress plugin.">
<header class="phero w"><p class="k">How it works</p><h1>Set up in 3 steps.</h1><p class="lede">Then customers upload art, see a price range, and approve your quote, right on your website.</p></header>
<section class="sec tight w"><Steps /></section>
<section class="sec w"><p class="k">The journey</p><h2>What your customers see.</h2><Journey /></section>
<section class="sec dark"><div class="w two"><div><p class="k">Works alongside your shop software</p><h2>Not an all-in-one. The step before.</h2></div><div><p class="bp">Keep your existing shop software for production and invoicing. OKtoPress handles the pre-job step: art upload, quote, signed proof and deposit (coming soon).</p>
  <div class="ctas"><a class="btn lg" href={SITE.signup}>Start free</a><a class="btn ghost lg" style="color:#fff!important;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.3)" href="/dpi-checker" data-pass-src>Try the art checker →</a></div></div></div></section>
</Base>
